\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. The day is past and over;
\par All thanks, O Lord, to Thee;
\par We pray Thee now that sinless
\par The hours of dark may be:
\par O Jesu, keep us in Thy sight,
\par And guard us through the coming night.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. The joys of day are over;
\par We lift our hearts to Thee,
\par And ask Thee that offenceless
\par The hours of dark may be:
\par O Jesu, make their darkness light,
\par And guard us through the coming night.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. The toils  of day are over;
\par We raise our hymns to Thee;
\par And ask that free from peril
\par The hours of dark may be:
\par O Jesu, keep us in Thy sight,
\par And guard us through the coming night.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. Be Thou our soul's Preserver,
\par For Thou, O God, dost know
\par How many are the perils 
\par Awaiting us below:
\par O loving Jesu, hear our call,
\par And guard and save us from them all.
\par              Amen.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\fs16 
\par }

